research/audit/wave6-real-analysis-limits.provenance.jsonl-9-{"id":"thm-convergence-iff-limsup-equals-liminf","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Limit_superior_and_limit_inferior"],"rationale":"The source states convergence in the extended real line iff liminf and limsup agree, with the common value equal to the limit, and separately records the plus/minus-infinity cases. The local proof is independently stratified.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave6-real-analysis-limits.provenance.jsonl-10-{"id":"thm-limsup-is-greatest-subsequential-limit","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://www.math.uci.edu/~ndonalds/math140a/notes.pdf","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Limit_superior_and_limit_inferior"],"rationale":"UCI states that the set of extended subsequential limits is nonempty and has supremum equal to limsup; the limsup/liminf source states limsup is the greatest cluster value in the extended line. The local proof constructs the witnessing subsequence canonically.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
